---
description: Approved visual language, accessibility, and Figma parity.
globs: src/**/*.{tsx,css}
alwaysApply: false
---

Read `docs/design-system.md` before UI work.

- Dark mode is implemented first; components must remain compatible with a future light mode.
- Use near-black charcoal, off-white, and restrained blood-red accents.
- Red is an intentional accent, not a default surface color.
- Prefer angular geometry and 0–4 px corner radii.
- Avoid glassmorphism, neon glow, glossy effects, heavy shadows, and decorative gradients.
- Use Archivo for display text and Inter for body/interface text.
- Timer numerals use tabular figures.
- Do not communicate status through color alone.
- Use visible focus states and approximately 44×44 px touch targets.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- User-facing strings are Polish and must not be hardcoded repeatedly across unrelated components.
- Match the reference screen first; propose improvements separately.
